{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-49655" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{7+6x-{x}^{2}}}\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14034005/state.json" "file_sha256" "056371f2ab91459c0778fcddee852e35ce6ff78064aa4586142eba1421ac4558"} {"question" "q-49655" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we complete the square for the argument of the square root in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7+6x-{x}^{2} & =-({x}^{2}-6x-7) \\\\  & =-({x}^{2}-2\\cdot 3x+[{3}^{2}-{3}^{2}]-7) \\\\  & =-((x-3)^{2}-16) \\\\  & =16-(x-3)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above in the given integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{7+6x-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{16-(x-3)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{16(1-(x-3)^{2}/16)}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{16}\\cdot \\sqrt{1-(x-3)^{2}/16}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{4\\sqrt{1-(x-3)^{2}/16}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-((x-3)/4)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis resembles the basic integral for inverse sine:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u+C\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $(\\frac{x-3}{4}).$\n\nSo, let's perform the substitution\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{x-3}{4}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{4}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=4\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the integral in terms of $u,$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{7+6x-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{4}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-((x-3)/4)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\cdot 4\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{x-3}{4})+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14034005/state.json" "file_sha256" "056371f2ab91459c0778fcddee852e35ce6ff78064aa4586142eba1421ac4558"} {"question" "q-49655" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14034005/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a820e6529020827fbb17306f95eea6a2f154af22cceb9ab7f5fdf02e33cf4aa8"} {"question" "q-49655" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14034005/state.json" "file_sha256" "056371f2ab91459c0778fcddee852e35ce6ff78064aa4586142eba1421ac4558"} {"question" "q-49655" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{x-3}{4})+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{x+4}{3})+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{x-4}{3})+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(x-3)+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{x-3}{4})+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14034005/state.json" "file_sha256" "056371f2ab91459c0778fcddee852e35ce6ff78064aa4586142eba1421ac4558"} {"question" "q-49655" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{x-3}{4})+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14034005/state.json" "file_sha256" "056371f2ab91459c0778fcddee852e35ce6ff78064aa4586142eba1421ac4558"} {"question" "q-348330" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{-1}^{-1/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{-x(x+2)}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14034005/state.json" "file_sha256" "056371f2ab91459c0778fcddee852e35ce6ff78064aa4586142eba1421ac4558"} {"question" "q-348330" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we complete the square for the argument of the square root in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-x(x+2) & =-({x}^{2}+2x) \\\\  & =-({x}^{2}+2\\cdot 1x+[{1}^{2}-{1}^{2}]) \\\\  & =-((x+1)^{2}-1) \\\\  & =1-(x+1)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the given integral, we get\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-1}^{-1/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{-x(x+2)}}\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{-1}^{-1/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(x+1)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThis resembles the basic integral for inverse sine:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u+C\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $(x+1).$\n\nSo, let's perform the substitution\n\n$$\nu=x+1.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nLet's use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $-1$ | $-1/2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $1/2$ |\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{-1/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{-x(x+2)}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u\\,{|}_{0}^{1/2} \\\\  & =arcsin\\,(\\frac{1}{2})-arcsin\\,(0) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{6}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14034005/state.json" "file_sha256" "056371f2ab91459c0778fcddee852e35ce6ff78064aa4586142eba1421ac4558"} {"question" "q-348330" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14034005/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a820e6529020827fbb17306f95eea6a2f154af22cceb9ab7f5fdf02e33cf4aa8"} {"question" "q-348330" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14034005/state.json" "file_sha256" "056371f2ab91459c0778fcddee852e35ce6ff78064aa4586142eba1421ac4558"} {"question" "q-348330" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\pi}{6}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14034005/state.json" "file_sha256" "056371f2ab91459c0778fcddee852e35ce6ff78064aa4586142eba1421ac4558"} {"question" "q-348531" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{5+\\sqrt{2}}^{7}\\frac{8}{|x-5|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-10x+24}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14034005/state.json" "file_sha256" "056371f2ab91459c0778fcddee852e35ce6ff78064aa4586142eba1421ac4558"} {"question" "q-348531" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we complete the square for the expression inside the square root:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-10x+24 & ={x}^{2}-2\\cdot 5x+({5}^{2}-{5}^{2})+24 \\\\  & =({x}^{2}-2\\cdot 5x+{5}^{2})-25+24 \\\\  & =(x-5)^{2}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the given integral, we get\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{5+\\sqrt{2}}^{7}\\frac{8}{|x-5|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-10x+24}}\\,\\text{d}x=8{\\int }_{5+\\sqrt{2}}^{7}\\frac{1}{|x-5|\\sqrt{(x-5)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThis resembles the basic integral for inverse secant:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\text{arcsec}\\,u+C\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $(x-5).$\n\nSo, let's perform the substitution\n\n$$\nu=x-5.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nLet's use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $5+\\sqrt{2}$ | $7$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $\\sqrt{2}$ | $2$ |\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{5+\\sqrt{2}}^{7}\\frac{8}{|x-5|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-10x+24}}\\,\\text{d}x & =8{\\int }_{\\sqrt{2}}^{2}\\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =8\\,\\text{arcsec}\\,u\\,{|}_{\\sqrt{2}}^{2} \\\\  & =8(\\text{arcsec}(2)-\\text{arcsec}(\\sqrt{2})) \\\\  & =8(\\frac{\\pi }{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14034005/state.json" "file_sha256" "056371f2ab91459c0778fcddee852e35ce6ff78064aa4586142eba1421ac4558"} {"question" "q-348531" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14034005/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a820e6529020827fbb17306f95eea6a2f154af22cceb9ab7f5fdf02e33cf4aa8"} {"question" "q-348531" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14034005/state.json" "file_sha256" "056371f2ab91459c0778fcddee852e35ce6ff78064aa4586142eba1421ac4558"} {"question" "q-348531" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2\\pi}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14034005/state.json" "file_sha256" "056371f2ab91459c0778fcddee852e35ce6ff78064aa4586142eba1421ac4558"} {"question" "q-348563" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{-7}^{\\sqrt{3}-6}\\frac{6}{{x}^{2}+12x+37}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14034005/state.json" "file_sha256" "056371f2ab91459c0778fcddee852e35ce6ff78064aa4586142eba1421ac4558"} {"question" "q-348563" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we complete the square in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+12x+37 & ={x}^{2}+2\\cdot 6x+({6}^{2}-{6}^{2})+37 \\\\  & =({x}^{2}+2\\cdot 6x+{6}^{2})-36+37 \\\\  & =(x+6)^{2}+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the denominator, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{6}{{x}^{2}+12x+37}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{6}{(x+6)^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6\\int \\frac{1}{1+(x+6)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis resembles the basic integral for inverse tangent:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $(x+6).$\n\nSo, let's perform the substitution\n\n$$\nu=x+6.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nLet's use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $-7$ | $\\sqrt{3}-6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $-1$ | $\\sqrt{3}$ |\n\nFinally, we write the integral in terms of $u,$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-7}^{\\sqrt{3}-6}\\frac{6}{{x}^{2}+12x+37}\\,\\text{d}x & =6{\\int }_{-1}^{\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =6\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u\\,{|}_{-1}^{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\  & =6(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\sqrt{3}-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-1)) \\\\  & =6(\\frac{\\pi }{3}-(-\\frac{\\pi }{4})) \\\\  & =6(\\frac{7\\pi }{12}) \\\\  & =\\frac{7\\pi }{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14034005/state.json" "file_sha256" "056371f2ab91459c0778fcddee852e35ce6ff78064aa4586142eba1421ac4558"} {"question" "q-348563" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14034005/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a820e6529020827fbb17306f95eea6a2f154af22cceb9ab7f5fdf02e33cf4aa8"} {"question" "q-348563" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14034005/state.json" "file_sha256" "056371f2ab91459c0778fcddee852e35ce6ff78064aa4586142eba1421ac4558"} {"question" "q-348563" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{7\\pi}{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14034005/state.json" "file_sha256" "056371f2ab91459c0778fcddee852e35ce6ff78064aa4586142eba1421ac4558"} {"question" "q-348572" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{4}^{5}\\frac{8}{{x}^{2}-8x+17}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14034005/state.json" "file_sha256" "056371f2ab91459c0778fcddee852e35ce6ff78064aa4586142eba1421ac4558"} {"question" "q-348572" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we complete the square in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-8x+17 & ={x}^{2}-2\\cdot 4x+({4}^{2}-{4}^{2})+17 \\\\  & =({x}^{2}-2\\cdot 4x+{4}^{2})-16+17 \\\\  & =(x-4)^{2}+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the denominator, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{8}{{x}^{2}-8x+17}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{8}{(x-4)^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =8\\int \\frac{1}{1+(x-4)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis resembles the basic integral for inverse tangent:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $(x-4).$\n\nSo, let's perform the substitution\n\n$$\nu=x-4.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nLet's use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $4$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, we write the integral in terms of $u,$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{4}^{5}\\frac{8}{{x}^{2}-8x+17}\\,\\text{d}x & =8{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =8\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u\\,{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =8(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(1)-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =8(\\frac{\\pi }{4}-0) \\\\  & =2\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14034005/state.json" "file_sha256" "056371f2ab91459c0778fcddee852e35ce6ff78064aa4586142eba1421ac4558"} {"question" "q-348572" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14034005/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a820e6529020827fbb17306f95eea6a2f154af22cceb9ab7f5fdf02e33cf4aa8"} {"question" "q-348572" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14034005/state.json" "file_sha256" "056371f2ab91459c0778fcddee852e35ce6ff78064aa4586142eba1421ac4558"} {"question" "q-348572" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2\\pi"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/r